</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McDonald</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Overhage</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Barnes</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><collab>INPC Management Committee</collab><etal/></person-group><article-title>The Indiana network for patient care: a working local health information infrastructure. An example of a working infrastructure collaboration that links data from five health systems and hundreds of millions of entries</article-title><source>Health Aff (Millwood)</source><year>2005</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>1214</fpage><lpage>1220</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1377/hlthaff.24.5.1214</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">McDonald CJ, Overhage JM, Barnes M, INPC Management Committee, et al. The Indiana network for patient care: a working local health information infrastructure. An example of a working infrastructure collaboration that links data from five health systems and hundreds of millions of entries. Health Aff (Millwood). 2005;24:1214&#x02013;20. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16162565</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eyestone</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Information technology in the foxhole</article-title><source>Top Health Inf Manage</source><year>1995</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>20</fpage><lpage>31</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Eyestone SM. Information technology in the foxhole. Top Health Inf Manage. 1995;16:20&#x02013;31. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10144371</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>